{"diagnosis": "Fetch NOP test traps with TRAP: no progress max_addr=0x00000000 for 2009 cycles, expected PC to advance sequentially through NOP memory. Every NOP (opcode 0010011, funct3 000) wrongly decodes with instr_jalr asserted instead of deasserted, causing a jump to 0 loop. Root cause is line 870 in picorv32.v where instr_jalr compares mem_rdata_latched[6:0] != 7'b1100111 instead of ==, inverting JALR decode.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picorv32.v b/picorv32.v
--- a/picorv32.v
+++ b/picorv32.v
@@ -867,7 +867,7 @@
 			instr_lui     <= mem_rdata_latched[6:0] == 7'b0110111;
 			instr_auipc   <= mem_rdata_latched[6:0] == 7'b0010111;
 			instr_jal     <= mem_rdata_latched[6:0] == 7'b1101111;
-			instr_jalr    <= mem_rdata_latched[6:0] != 7'b1100111 && mem_rdata_latched[14:12] == 3'b000;
+			instr_jalr    <= mem_rdata_latched[6:0] == 7'b1100111 && mem_rdata_latched[14:12] == 3'b000;
 			instr_retirq  <= mem_rdata_latched[6:0] == 7'b0001011 && mem_rdata_latched[31:25] == 7'b0000010 && ENABLE_IRQ;
 			instr_waitirq <= mem_rdata_latched[6:0] == 7'b0001011 && mem_rdata_latched[31:25] == 7'b0000100 && ENABLE_IRQ;

", "expected": "tohost PASS (not FAIL 0xdead), TRAP: no progress cleared with max_addr advancing beyond 0x00000000"}

